module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_rule_is_applied_at_the_site_that_prompted_it_and_not_its_sibling

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_rule_is_applied_at_the_site_that_prompted_it_and_not_its_sibling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_rule_is_applied_at_the_site_that_prompted_it_and_not_its_sibling" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a rule is applied at the site that prompted it and not its sibling: an author states or receives a rule while repairing one arm, applies it correctly THERE, and leaves a structurally identical arm beside it unchanged -- with no reason for the difference. The invalid state is a program in which one arm enforces a rule and its sibling does not, where nothing about either arm explains why. The harm is not the unenforced arm alone: THE ENFORCED ARM MAKES THE UNENFORCED ONE LOOK COVERED, so a reader who checks the first stops looking, and the class survives every repair of its own instances.",

    "WHY IT IS NOT INATTENTION, which is the diagnosis that makes it fileable rather than a note to try harder. A RULE ARRIVES ATTACHED TO THE INSTANCE THAT PRODUCED IT -- a review finding, a ruling, an author's own argument -- and nothing in the workflow walks the siblings. The author who has just reasoned the rule out is the best-placed person to apply it corpus-wide and the least likely to, because the reasoning terminates when the prompting instance is fixed. Each instance is also cheap to fix locally, so the pattern is invisible from inside any one lane and visible only across lanes.",

    "SPECIMEN SET, gunbc#12049, five corrections of this shape in ONE module over one day, each found by a reviewer or a ruling rather than by the author. (1) `AttainUnreached` routed to its own finding on the direct comparison arm and NOT on the rename arm, so a rename whose target nothing could look at reported as `RenameTargetBelowBaseline` -- the rename lowered the bar -- when nothing had looked at it. (2) The verdict gained a `ProgressUnobserved` arm while the FINDINGS below it went on reporting every baseline row as vanished-and-owing-a-disposition. (3) A bar and a reading shared one type, so an unreached BAR answered the comparison exactly as an unreached READING once had. (4) `AttainRefused` carried a stage and discarded the cause it already held; `AttainDiverged` discarded its cause in the same edit. (5) A disposition roster built AFTER its author argued classify-versus-waive explicitly admitted on `Present { value: _ } => []`, while the roster written under the same requirement an hour later classified correctly.",

    "THE SHARPEST FORM IS A DISPOSITION FIELD WITH A VOCABULARY ON IT, from specimen (5). The roster offered two named, well-argued arms and admitted on ANY declaration, so an author declaring `PriorAcceptanceWasNeverSound` over an acceptance that WAS sound got a silent pass. That is harder to spot than a missing check, because THE VOCABULARY IS THE THING THAT MAKES A READER STOP LOOKING: a named arm reads as a decision that was made.",

    "THIS IS NOT `symptom_link_patched_without_the_earliest_unjustified_boundary`, and the discriminator is mechanical. That class is about a repair made at the WRONG LAYER -- the link where the symptom appeared rather than the earliest unjustified boundary. Here EVERY repair is at the right layer and correct on its own terms; what is missing is the OTHER SITE at the same layer. A fix that root-causes perfectly and lands on one of two identical arms is this class and not that one. Nor is it `transport_defect_repaired_at_one_call_site`, whose repair encodes a transport fact in a caller; these repairs encode nothing wrong, they are merely incomplete.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, and it is addressed to the author rather than to a reviewer because the author is the one holding the rule: WHEN YOU APPLY A RULE, ASK WHAT ELSE IS SHAPED LIKE THE THING YOU JUST FIXED. Concretely -- the other arm of the same match, the other roster under the same requirement, the other importer of the symbol you narrowed, the other caller of the function whose contract you tightened, the other direction of the join you made exact. The tell that the question was never asked is a diff that touches exactly the site named in the finding. A second tell, available to a reviewer: a rule stated in prose on a carrier, enforced by a check on one path, with a structurally identical path carrying the same prose and no check.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: mechanically preventable, and not higher, because 'structurally identical arm' is not decidable in general -- two arms may look alike and differ for a reason the corpus does not carry. What IS decidable is the narrow, high-value case: a coproduct match whose arms call different folds where one fold's name differs only by the arm it serves, and a roster type whose consumers pattern-match `{ value: _ }` where a sibling roster of the same shape matches its variants. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a lens over the `Node` tree that reports, for each coproduct match, the arms whose bodies are structurally identical modulo the bound variables, beside the arms whose bodies diverge -- the divergences are the population to read, and an arm calling a strictly smaller fold than its sibling is the shape that found all five specimens above.",

    "ONE CROSS-LANE FACT, because it is the argument for reporting an instance BEFORE fixing it rather than after. The same shape was observed four further times on 2026-09-22 in other lanes -- a prose claim enforced on one path and not its twin, a graft alias narrowed at three call sites and left at two importers, a fail-open default surviving inside the fix that removed the fail-open beside it -- and the generalisation arrived from whoever happened to be holding the fourth instance, both for this class and for the net-count class found the same day. A FIXED INSTANCE IS NEARLY INVISIBLE TO EVERYONE ELSE, so a lane that repairs quietly removes the evidence that would have made the class visible.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
